 thinning might be a little small.&#13;&#13;- When presenting the probabilistic solution to the inverse problem I would always recommend to present a number \(e.g. 9\) of posterior realizations.  T\he mean+ std dev may not be a good summary of the posterior pdf.&#13;&#13;- To show the information gained from the data show histograms/pdfs for the TWIP, from prior and posterior realizations.&#13;&#13;Best regards,&#13;&#13;chris</span></p></body>)/Rect[230.183 795.853 254.183 819.853]/Subj(Sticky Note)/Subtype/Text/T(Chris Finlay)/Type/Annot>>endobj2090 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Parent 2089 0 R/Rect[595.276 727.853 779.276 819.853]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj2092 0 obj
